  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Thrive Tajikistan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Tajikistan):  Thrive Tajikistan, a Global Development Alliance (GDA) with the Aga Khan Foundation (AKF) will leverage resources and collective strengths to enhance the quality of life of people living in all 16 districts of Khatlon region and Gorno-Badakhshan Autonomous Oblast (GBAO) along the Tajik-Afghan border. Thrive will support local and sub-national governance institutions to manage resources and social services, particularly through strengthening sub-national governance entities in Khatlon and GBAO. The program will continue to support the capacity of local government entities to support community development projects; provide financing and technical assistance for micro-development projects; support producer groups, and provide technical assistance to both farmers and agricultural input providers to increase their productivity. To further address the economic challenges of communities in the target areas, Thrive will extend its support to aspiring and existing entrepreneurs through entrepreneurship and social entrepreneurship training, business incubation and acceleration, and access to innovative capital. Finally, the activity will support the construction and rehabilitation of drinking water supply systems and public latrines. The water systems will introduce metering systems, which by linking water fees with actual use will improve sustainability of the system.  Thrive contributes to $350,000 of the Mission&apos;s $3.5 million DRG earmark. .The program supports ICS goal 3.1, and the CAS by strengthening the sovereignty and independence of the Central Asian states, individually and as a group..</narrative>
  </description>
